.TH SDL_GetTrayMenuParentTray 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetTrayMenuParentTray \- Gets the tray for which this menu is the first-level menu, if the current menu isn\(aqt a submenu.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Tray * SDL_GetTrayMenuParentTray(SDL_TrayMenu *menu);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Either this function or
.BR SDL_GetTrayMenuParentEntry ()
will return non-NULL for any given menu\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I menu
the menu for which to get the parent enttrayry\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the parent tray, or NULL if this menu is a submenu\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called on the thread that created the tray\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateTrayMenu (3),
.BR SDL_GetTrayMenuParentEntry (3)
